  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given hyperbola is<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& 9 x^2-16 y^2-36 x+96 y-252=0 \\\\<br />& \\Rightarrow 9\\left(x^2-4 x\\right)-16\\left(y^2-6 y\\right)=252 \\\\<br />& \\Rightarrow 9\\left(x^2-4 x+4\\right)-16\\left(y^2-6 y+9\\right) \\\\<br />& =252+36-144 \\\\<br />& \\Rightarrow 9(x-2)^2-16(y-3)^2=144<br />\\end{aligned}$<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/jLY8-6clWoBW7M9aqoLEdPXjxPnZv_kpDKECzHGVaUY.original.fullsize.png\"><br><br />Put $x=X+2$ and $y=Y+3$<br />$\\therefore$ Equation (i) becomes $\\frac{X^2}{16}-\\frac{Y^2}{9}=1$<br />Now, vertices are $X= \\pm a$ wehre $a=4$ and $Y=0$<br />Hence, vertices are $(6,3),(-2,3)$.",
    "image": null
  },
